import Mathlib
import CombinatorialGroupTheory_Magnus_2004.Chap02.Proposition_2_5_14

-- Declarations for this item will be appended below by the statement pipeline.

universe u

section

variable {F : Type u} [Group F] [IsFreeGroup F]

open Subgroup (normalClosure)

-- Primary domain: primitive elements in free groups, singleton normal closures, and conjugacy.
/- Layer triage:
- `source-facing`: a primitive element `p` of a free group and an element `q : F`, with the
  intersection `⟪q⟫ ∩ ⟪p⟫` not contained in the commutator subgroup `[F, F]`.
- `core/canonical`: the chapter owner predicate `IsPrimitiveElement`, together with
  `Subgroup.normalClosure` for normal closures, `commutator F` for the commutator subgroup, and
  `IsConj` for conjugacy.
- `bridge/view`: a chosen basis element `basis x` is a bridge witness for `IsPrimitiveElement`,
  via `FreeGroupBasis.isPrimitiveElement`, and Proposition `2-5-14` supplies the owner-level
  bridge from membership in `normalClosure ({q} : Set F)` to the conjugacy conclusion.
- Domain sampling:
  1. `IsPrimitiveElement` from `CombinatorialGroupTheory.Basic` is the project owner for
     “belongs to some free basis”, so the proposition should not expose a parallel basis-witness
     theorem as its main entry.
  2. `FreeGroupBasis.isPrimitiveElement` is the canonical project bridge from a chosen basis
     element to that owner predicate.
  3. `Subgroup.normalClosure` and `Subgroup.normalClosure_subset_iff` are mathlib's owner API for
     normal closures of subsets and their containment relation.
  4. `_root_.commutator F` is mathlib's canonical owner for the derived subgroup `[F, F]`.
  5. `IsConj` from `Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Conj` is mathlib's owner relation for conjugacy.
  6. `conjugate_or_conjugate_inv_of_mem_normalClosure_of_isPrimitiveElement` from Proposition
     `2-5-14` is the direct chapter bridge theorem in the same domain.
- Primitive vs. derived:
  the primitive public data are the element `p`, its owner-side primitivity hypothesis, and the
  element `q`; any chosen basis and index witnessing primitivity are bridge data rather than part
  of the main theorem surface. The current item is therefore still `source-facing`, while the
  chosen basis witness and Proposition `2-5-14` remain `bridge/view` proof input. -/
-- The numbered proposition is exposed directly at the owner level `IsPrimitiveElement`; a
-- basis-element formulation would only restate the standard bridge
-- `FreeGroupBasis.isPrimitiveElement`.

/-- Proposition 2-5-15: if `q` and a primitive element `p` of a free group have singleton normal
closures whose intersection is not contained in the commutator subgroup, then `q` is conjugate to
`p` or to `p⁻¹`. -/
-- Proof sketch: this item is the bridge from the abelianized intersection hypothesis to the
-- owner predicate `IsPrimitiveElement`. Choose a basis witness for `p`, reduce to the
-- corresponding basis element, show that the noncontainment hypothesis forces that basis element
-- into the singleton normal closure generated by `q`, and then apply Proposition `2-5-14`.
theorem conjugate_or_conjugate_inv_of_inf_normalClosure_not_le_commutator_of_isPrimitiveElement
    (p q : F) (hp : IsPrimitiveElement p)
    (hinter :
      ¬ normalClosure ({q} : Set F) ⊓ normalClosure ({p} : Set F) ≤ commutator F) :
    IsConj q p ∨ IsConj q p⁻¹ := sorry

end
